  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Desk",
    "overview": "Hookworthy is a writer's desk at 11 PM. The ground is near-black, the page sits a step lighter on it, cards are quiet greys edged with hairlines, and one light pill does the asking. Newsreader sets the one big line on a page; Inter carries everything you read and press; Geist Mono only keeps time, counts and addresses. There is no brand hue. Colour is spent on meaning: an amber wavy line under soft words, green for better, red for wrong. Dark is the default theme, and light is the same system inverted (white cards on a soft grey desk, an ink pill).\n\nPersonality comes from people and from the product, never from decoration. Real portraits and platform marks sit inside the headlines as small tilted tiles that turn over; the app itself works in a window under the hero; photographs carry the story. Each page gets exactly one sheet of the other theme: on the homepage, the \"11 PM thought\" chapter is paper on a dark page (and night on a light one), and the Pro plan card wears the same sheet. Two-tone heads (ink, then grey) are saved for that chapter, pricing and the close.\n\nThe site is generous (sections open with clamp(104px, 15vh, 168px) of air and a 1200px measure); the app is compact (13.5–14px UI, 34px controls, an inset panel on a darker desk). Confirmed rejections from the brief: eyebrows and kickers, logo walls, testimonials, icon-card grids, and any promise of reach.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black desk and page, grey cards with 1px inset hairlines, ink #EDEDED; no pure white text, no hue for its own sake.",
      "One light pill per view; everything else is a hairline outline or a 7% ink tint.",
      "Newsreader 400 for the one big line, Inter for the rest, Geist Mono only for times, counts and URLs.",
      "Faces and platform marks set inside headlines as tilted tiles.",
      "One inverted sheet per page; the Pro card wears it too.",
      "Amber wavy line for soft words, green only for better, status as plain words with neutral dots.",
      "The product shown working, in a window, with an example account named as such."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Lamp Rule",
        "body": "One light pill per view carries the main action. Every other button is a hairline outline or a 7% ink tint. If two solid pills compete on one screen, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Rule",
        "body": "Amber means \"soft, look again\", green means \"better\", red means \"wrong\". Nothing is coloured to decorate, and status reads as a word and a neutral dot.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Sheet Rule",
        "body": "A page gets one inverted chapter, and the Pro plan card wears the same sheet. Never two chapters, never a coloured block.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Replica Rule",
        "body": "Platform colours never leave a replica or a platform tile, and Hookworthy greys never recolour one.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Big Line Rule",
        "body": "Newsreader appears only at 30px and up, at weight 400, roman. Below that, everything is Inter. A serif at body size or in bold is a mistake.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Tone Rule",
        "body": "A head may turn from ink to grey (`ink-3`) partway only in three places: the story chapter (\"From an 11 PM thought / to Tuesday morning.\"), pricing (\"Free to start. / Pro when you post daily.\") and the close (\"End of the page. / Start of the post.\"). Everywhere else a head is one colour.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Clock Rule",
        "body": "Mono is for times, counts, URLs, keys and step numbers, always with tabular figures; never a sentence.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-First Rule",
        "body": "Edges are 1px inset hairlines. A shadow means the thing floats; a resting card has none.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Frost-Over-Something Rule",
        "body": "Backdrop blur (18–20px) is only for a surface over a photograph or scrolling content. Nothing is frosted for looks.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Neutral Light Rule",
        "body": "The only light effects are the two ink-tinted pools behind the hero and under the window. No coloured glow, no glow on hover.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** set the one big line on a page in Newsreader 400, roman, tracked -0.022em to -0.04em; set everything else in Inter.",
      "**Do** put people and platforms inside the headline as tilted tiles (.84em, ±4°) that turn over while the line is on screen.",
      "**Do** show the product working in a frame, with heycape named as the example account in a caption.",
      "**Do** keep one light pill per view; make every other button a hairline outline or a 7% ink tint.",
      "**Do** mark soft words with the amber wavy underline (1.5px, offset 4–5px) and use amber for nothing larger than a badge.",
      "**Do** keep green for \"better\": a sharper line, a positive delta, Resolved, a scheduled check.",
      "**Do** write status as a plain word with a 6px neutral dot (filled done, hollow open).",
      "**Do** give a page exactly one inverted sheet, and let the Pro plan card wear it.",
      "**Do** ease UI with cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1), and keep the spring (cubic-bezier(.34,1.45,.5,1)) for things that land: tiles, the post chip, the count badge.",
      "**Do** pause every loop when it's off screen or the tab is hidden, and show the finished frame under reduced motion.",
      "**Do** render every post as its platform does, with a portrait, name, handle, time and counts."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put eyebrows or kickers above headings, on the site or in the app.",
      "**Don't** add logo walls, testimonials, icon-card grids, or any promise of reach or followers.",
      "**Don't** split a head into ink and grey outside the story chapter, pricing and the close.",
      "**Don't** introduce a brand hue, a coloured block or a gradient fill; there is no accent colour.",
      "**Don't** use gradient text or coloured glows; the only light is the two ink-tinted pools behind the hero and under the window.",
      "**Don't** frost a surface unless it sits over a photograph or scrolling content.",
      "**Don't** use side-stripe accents on cards or callouts; the one side rule is the 2px commenter-colour bar on a quoted excerpt.",
      "**Don't** set sentences in mono, or Newsreader below 30px or in bold.",
      "**Don't** use real people's names, faces or posts without permission, or put verified badges on fictional accounts.",
      "**Don't** auto-scroll content (no marquees)."
